an class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">lb</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Ground Chicken</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Main protein for the dish.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Smoked Paprika</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Adds a smoky flavor.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Garlic Powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For flavor.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Onion Powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For flavor.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Dried Oregano</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For flavor.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">½</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Cayenne Pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For heat.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To taste.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">½</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Black Pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To taste.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Olive Oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For cooking.</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-11430-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"11430\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Skillet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cooking the chicken chorizo.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-11430-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-11430-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"11430\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11430-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: In a mixing bowl, combine ground chicken with smoked paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, oregano, cayenne, salt, and pepper. Mix thoroughly until spices are evenly distributed.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11430-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Form the mixture into patties or sausage links. Make them as thick or thin as you like!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11430-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Cook the patties or links for 6–8 minutes per side, or until golden brown and cooked through.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11430-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Serve hot in tacos, sandwiches, or alongside eggs. Enjoy your flavorful chicken chorizo!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-11430-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>250</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>25g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>2g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients to create a delicious chicken <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chorizo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chorizo </a>dish packed with flavor!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Chicken-Chorizo.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for chicken chorizo displayed on a kitchen table, including ground chicken, spices, and olive oil.\" class=\"wp-image-11428\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Chicken-Chorizo.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Chicken-Chorizo-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Ground Chicken</strong> – 1 lb</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Smoked Paprika</strong> – 2 tsp</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Garlic Powder</strong> – 1 tsp</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Onion Powder</strong> – 1 tsp</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Dried Oregano</strong> – 1 tsp</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Cayenne Pepper</strong> – ½ tsp</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt</strong> – 1 tsp</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Black Pepper</strong> – ½ tsp</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Olive Oil</strong> – 1 tbsp</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-chicken-chorizo\"><strong>How to Make Chicken Chorizo</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This easy chicken chorizo recipe takes just 10 minutes to prepare and 15-20 minutes to cook. With a total time of about 30 minutes, you’ll have a delicious, spicy dish ready to enjoy!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Homemade-Chicken-Chorizo-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making chicken chorizo, including mixing ingredients, forming patties, cooking in a skillet, and serving in tacos.\" class=\"wp-image-11429\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Homemade-Chicken-Chorizo-Preparation.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Homemade-Chicken-Chorizo-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Combine Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a mixing bowl, combine ground chicken with smoked paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, oregano, cayenne, salt, and pepper. Mix thoroughly until spices are evenly distributed.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Form Patties or Links</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Form the mixture into patties or sausage links. Make them as thick or thin as you like!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Cook in Skillet</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Cook the patties or links for 6–8 minutes per side, or until golden brown and cooked through.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Serve and Enjoy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Serve hot in tacos, sandwiches, or alongside eggs. Enjoy your flavorful chicken chorizo!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Mexican</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>30 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>High Protein</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>In tacos, sandwiches, or alongside eggs!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-chicken-chorizo\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Chicken Chorizo</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Choose high-quality chicken for the best flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use fresh herbs like cilantro for a vibrant finish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Adjust the spice level by adding more or less chorizo.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the dish rest for a few minutes before serving to enhance flavors.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a squeeze of lime for a zesty kick.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-chicken-chorizo\"><strong>How to Serve this chicken chorizo</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve over fluffy rice or quinoa for a hearty meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with warm tortillas for delicious tacos.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with fresh avocado slices and cilantro for a refreshing touch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a side of black beans or corn salad for extra flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a dollop of Greek yogurt or sour cream to balance the spice.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with lime wedges for a zesty kick.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can prepare and store chicken chorizo for later enjoyment:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow chicken chorizo to cool completely.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the dish completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use freezer-safe containers or bags.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a skillet over medium heat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of chicken broth for moisture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat until warmed through, about 5-7 minutes.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is chicken chorizo made of?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Chicken chorizo is typically made from ground chicken mixed with a variety of spices, including paprika, garlic, and chili powder. This combination gives it a rich flavor and a slightly spicy kick, making it a delicious alternative to traditional chorizo. You can also find chicken chorizo that includes additional ingredients like herbs and vinegar for added depth of flavor.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Is chicken chorizo healthier than pork chorizo?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, chicken chorizo is generally considered to be a healthier option compared to pork chorizo. It tends to be lower in fat and calories, making it a great choice for those looking to reduce their fat intake while still enjoying the bold flavors of chorizo. Additionally, chicken is a leaner protein source, which can contribute to a balanced diet.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What exactly is chorizo?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Chorizo is a type of spicy sausage that originates from Spain and is made from pork, but there are many variations, including chicken chorizo. It is seasoned with a variety of spices, most notably smoked paprika, which gives it a distinctive flavor and vibrant color. Chorizo can be used in a variety of dishes, from tacos to stews, adding a deliciously spicy kick to any meal.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Is chicken chorizo spicy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Chicken chorizo can be spicy, depending on the specific recipe and the amount of chili used in the seasoning. Generally, it has a mild to moderate heat level, making it accessible for those who enjoy a bit of spice without overwhelming heat. If you prefer a milder flavor, you can always adjust the spices to suit your taste!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We hope you’re as excited to try this Easy Chicken Chorizo recipe as we are! It’s a delightful dish that brings warmth and flavor to your table in just 30 minutes. So gather your loved ones, savor each bite, and enjoy the simple joy of cooking together. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
